{
  "version": 1,
  "comments": {
    "c1": {
      "anchor": "i67",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "⌘Z and ⇧⌘Z are registered twice on the editor's page, the newer winning: ⌘Z may go to the wrong history",
      "excerpt": "⌘Z and ⇧⌘Z are registered twice on the editor's page, the newer winning: ⌘Z may go to the wrong history",
      "text": "What's the fix for this?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-14T05:02:57.418Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-14T05:04:20.054Z",
          "html": "<p>It's not a wrong-history bug:  the program's ⌘Z sits over the editor's on purpose and asks the editor first, so Edit undoes the editor's change and Run the program's.  The fix is to tell Spell UI's keyboard that layering is meant, so it stops warning:  written up in I67.  Press Do this to build it.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-14T05:03:33.618Z"
      }
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "i54",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "Autocomplete doesn't work in the code pane: <act should offer action",
      "excerpt": "Autocomplete doesn't work in the code pane: <act should offer action",
      "text": "This is working.\nIt would be even cooler if, on a tag basis somehow, it new that action was always a singleton tag, and tabbing on `<act` wrote out `<action \"\" />` with the cursor between the quotes",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-14T05:11:29.429Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-14T05:11:59.295Z",
          "html": "<p>Good idea:  filed as I70 and being built now.  Each tag will say how it's written:  <code>&lt;action \"\"/&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;divider/&gt;</code> close themselves (the caret between the quotes, or after the tag), a tag that holds things opens and closes around the caret.  Spell's own tags first, then Spell UI's from what each one's vocabulary says it holds.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-14T05:11:41.562Z"
      }
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "i55",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "Typing a property on an object or tag should show help for it, as you type",
      "excerpt": "Typing a property on an object or tag should show help for it, as you type",
      "text": "this is working, but it would be cooler if e.g. in `<segment ` and I selected `color` from the menu, it put `color=\"\"` and the cursor was between the quotes, and then it showed me the possible values for color",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-14T05:14:29.427Z",
